-- comp-05-knowledge — "Each employee has Knowledge that reaches a prompt."
--
-- 14 of 66 active employees had a profession-layer agent_knowledge row of their own. The other 52
-- had NOTHING, and the reason nobody noticed is in fn_agent_context itself: LAYER 2 falls back to a
-- DEPT-MATE's knowledge when an employee has none. So the Accounts Payable Specialist was handed
-- the CFO's expertise, the Graphic Designer was handed the Content Strategist's, and the block was
-- always present — which is exactly the failure mode this spec file exists to catch. A block that
-- renders is not the same claim as an employee who knows something.
--
-- Worse, the fallback needs at least one dept-mate WITH knowledge, and for 14 employees no such
-- person existed: whole departments reached zero profession knowledge and the prompt simply had no
-- LAYER 2 at all.
--
-- One profession row per employee, keyed to what THAT job actually has to know, grounded in the
-- business as it really is: a UAE B2B anonymous quotation marketplace, 3% customer reveal fee,
-- suppliers pay nothing until 31 Jul 2027, no off-platform contact before reveal, Mon-Fri working
-- days, one human founder. Written as operating knowledge, not as a job description — a row that
-- restates the title teaches nobody anything.
--
-- Idempotent: guarded by not exists on (agent_key, layer='profession'), so re-running adds nothing
-- and never duplicates. Existing rows are left alone.

-- agent_knowledge.id has a sequence that is BEHIND its own max(id) — the first insert attempted
-- id=1 against 1,869 existing rows. Rows were loaded at some point with explicit ids and the
-- sequence was never advanced, so every insert into this table has been failing on a duplicate key
-- and nobody noticed because nothing had inserted into it. Re-synchronise before writing; setval to
-- max(id) is idempotent, so this is safe on the project where the sequence is already correct.
-- pg_get_serial_sequence() returns NULL here: the sequence is not OWNED BY the column, it is only
-- named in its default, so the obvious one-liner silently does nothing and the next insert fails on
-- id=2 instead of id=1. Read the sequence out of the column default instead.
do $seq$
declare v_def text; v_seq text;
begin
  select pg_get_expr(d.adbin, d.adrelid) into v_def
    from pg_attrdef d
    join pg_attribute a on a.attrelid = d.adrelid and a.attnum = d.adnum
   where d.adrelid = 'public.agent_knowledge'::regclass and a.attname = 'id';
  v_seq := substring(v_def from '''([^'']+)''');
  if v_seq is not null then
    perform setval(v_seq::regclass,
                   greatest(coalesce((select max(id) from public.agent_knowledge), 1), 1), true);
  end if;
end $seq$;

insert into public.agent_knowledge
  (agent_key, topic, content, priority, layer, source_ref, owner_agent, version,
   confidence, validation_status, review_due)
select v.agent_key, v.topic, v.content, 74, 'profession',
       'session16:profession-backfill', 'knowledge_director', 1,
       0.60, 'unvalidated', (current_date + 365)
  from (values

-- ── customer_success ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
('cs_onboarding','Customer onboarding on an anonymous marketplace',
 'First-job activation is the only onboarding metric that matters: a customer who posts one inquiry and never returns has not been onboarded. Sequence: confirm the brief is complete enough to quote (category, emirate, scope, quantity, timeline), explain the anonymity rule before they ask (no supplier identity, no contact details, no off-platform conversation until they pay the 3% reveal fee), and set the expectation on timing in WORKING days (Mon-Fri; Sat/Sun do not count). The commonest drop-off is a customer who expects to talk to suppliers directly and reads anonymity as evasion — answer it as protection: they compare price and scope without being chased. Never promise a quote count or a turnaround the marketplace has not measured.'),
('cs_retention','Retention and win-back for repeat B2B buyers',
 'Retention on this platform is job-driven, not subscription-driven: the trigger for a second inquiry is a completed first job, so retention work starts at completion, not at renewal. Segment on outcome, not recency — a customer whose job completed and who has not returned in 60 days is a different problem from one whose supplier went non-responsive and was refunded. For the latter the recovery is the refund plus the non-response charge already billed to the supplier; lead with what the platform did about it. Never win back with a discount on the reveal fee: it is the only revenue line and discounting it teaches customers to wait.'),
('cs_support','Support on a pre-reveal anonymous marketplace',
 'The three tickets that account for most volume: "where are my quotes" (check the inquiry is rfq_ready and routed, not that suppliers are slow), "who is this supplier" (identity is withheld until the reveal fee is paid — this is the product, not a limitation), and "the supplier I paid to reveal is not answering". The third has a defined remedy and it must be quoted exactly: if a revealed supplier does not respond within 3 working days and the founder also cannot reach them, the customer reveal fee is REFUNDED and a non-response charge equal to that fee is billed to the supplier. Do not invent goodwill credits, do not quote an AED 250 admin fee to customers (it is founder-set and not in the customer terms), and never state a commission — there is none.'),
('rfq_success','Making an RFQ answerable',
 'Most RFQs that die, die at the brief. A quotable brief needs: category, emirate, scope or BoQ, quantity or area, timeline, and the access or site constraint that changes price. Chase the missing field before dispatch, not after: an RFQ sent to ten suppliers with an unanswerable brief burns supplier goodwill ten times and returns nothing. Watch for the two silent killers — a category that no approved supplier serves (a coverage problem, escalate to Marketplace OS, do not keep resending) and a customer budget an order of magnitude off the category median (a expectation problem, correct it before quoting). Success is one submitted, comparable quote, not ten dispatches.'),

-- ── evolution ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
('innovation_mgr','Running change against a live company with one founder',
 'Every proposed change competes for one scarce resource: founder attention. Rank proposals by (metric moved x confidence) / founder minutes required, and kill anything that cannot name a metric and its baseline BEFORE it is built — an improvement without a baseline can never be graded and becomes permanent. The company already records this properly: outcome_record carries baseline_value, expected_direction, due_at and a verdict, and fn_outcome_evaluate grades it. Any change you propose that is not written into that table is untracked by construction. Prefer reversible changes; prefer the change that removes a step over the one that adds a check.'),
('optimisation_eng','Cost and latency optimisation of an AI-run company',
 'The spend is per-call, metered into ai_cost_log with model_used, tier, tokens, cached and could_be_cheaper on every row. Optimise in this order, because it is the order of effect: (1) do not make the call at all — cache, or answer from stored state; (2) make it once — dedupe by cache_hit_key; (3) make it smaller — trim the prompt, not the answer; (4) make it cheaper — drop a tier only where could_be_cheaper is already true and the task class tolerates it. Degrading a tier to save cost on a money, legal or safety path is not an optimisation, it is a risk transfer. Departments have budgets with a degrade threshold and a halt ceiling; hitting the ceiling stops non-critical spend, so watch the burn rate, not the total.'),
('org_designer','Designing an organisation of AI employees',
 'The unit of design is the RESPONSIBILITY, not the department: exactly one owner per responsibility, enforced structurally (os_responsibility has a primary key on responsibility alone, so a second owner is unrepresentable). When work needs two OSes, that is an interface, not a shared owner — declare it on os_interface and route it over the event bus, never by giving both a copy of the work. Signs the design is wrong: a task that bounces between departments (missing owner), an employee with no KPI (unmeasurable role), a department whose queue only grows (capacity or authority too low). Authority is the other half of a role — an employee with responsibilities and no matching grant escalates everything and the founder becomes the bottleneck.'),

-- ── exec ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
('ceo','Running a marketplace that has not launched',
 'Pre-launch, the only two numbers that matter are supply depth per category and time-to-first-quote; revenue is an output of those and cannot be forced. The economics are fixed and asymmetric: customers pay 3% of the quotation value on reveal, suppliers pay nothing until 31 Jul 2027 (the first 1,000 registrants never pay), so growth capital is spent on SUPPLY and monetisation follows demand. Do not trade anonymity for volume — it is the product. The company runs itself through ten Operating Systems and an event bus; your job is to change what the company is working on, not to do the work: read v_os_health, act on the worst figure, and record the decision with its reasoning so it can be graded later. Capital, identity, security and legal judgement are founder gates and always will be.'),
('cpo','Product on a two-sided anonymous marketplace',
 'Both sides must be designed against the same constraint: no identity and no contact before the reveal. That forces the product to carry everything the decision needs INSIDE the quote — scope, exclusions, lead time, validity, warranty, payment terms — because the buyer cannot ring up to ask. Every field you add to the quote form is a field a supplier may abandon on; every field you remove is a comparison the buyer cannot make. Measure the funnel at three points only: inquiry to rfq_ready, rfq_ready to first submitted quote, quote to paid reveal. A product change that does not move one of those three is a preference. The 3% fee is charged on reveal, so anything that increases quotes-per-inquiry increases revenue directly.'),
('strategy_director','Turning strategy into measurable objectives',
 'An objective without a computable measure is a slogan and will never be graded — this company had 50 of them, whose "measure" was a label like "gl_journal" or "qualified pipeline". A usable objective names the horizon (strategic, annual, quarterly, weekly, daily), the number, and the SQL that returns it; os_objective.measure_sql and company_goals.measure_sql are where that lives. Cascade downward without re-inventing: an employee KPI should serve a department objective which serves a company goal, and employee_kpi.serves_goal / serves_objective exist to make that link checkable. Beware the measure that is right for the wrong reason: revenue measured as a count of inquiries reads 0 today and would read nonsense tomorrow.'),

-- ── finance ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
('ap_specialist','Accounts payable in a UAE sole establishment',
 'Three-way match before anything is scheduled: invoice against the commitment, against what was actually received, and against the approved budget line. QuotesDone is NOT VAT-registered (no TRN), so an invoice charging you UAE VAT still gets paid but the VAT is a cost, not a recoverable input — do not book it as recoverable. Every payable posts to gl_journal with a source and a source_ref; an entry that is not posted is not reconciled, and the daily objective is zero unposted entries. Watch duplicate invoices on re-sent PDFs (match on supplier + amount + invoice number, not on file name) and never pay a bank account that changed by email without a verified callback — supplier bank details live on the lead record with the IBAN document behind them.'),
('financial_analyst','Financial analysis of a pre-revenue marketplace',
 'The revenue formula is single-line and must never be approximated: 3% reveal fee on the quotation value, charged when the customer reveals, net of confirmed refunds. Suppliers contribute nothing until 1 Aug 2027, and the first 1,000 registrants never contribute, so do not model supplier subscription in year one. Unit economics therefore reduce to (paid reveals) x (3% x average quotation value) minus the AI cost of getting there, which is metered per call in ai_cost_log — cost per completed RFQ is a real, computable number and the only sensible efficiency metric. Runway is cash divided by monthly opex where opex is dominated by AI spend, so a model-tier change is a runway change. Treat any actual of zero as a fact about the launch, not as a broken query, but check the query anyway.'),

-- ── hr ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
('culture_performance_mgr','Performance management of AI employees',
 'Performance here is measurable in a way human performance is not: every employee has KPIs with measure_sql, an authority grant, a task queue with a cap, and a full audit trail of decisions. Judge on three things and nothing else — output against KPI, escalation quality (did they escalate what genuinely exceeded their authority, and NOT what did not), and whether the loop closed (outcome measured, lesson recorded, playbook improved). Two failure patterns dominate: the employee who escalates everything (authority too narrow, fix the grant, not the employee) and the employee who never escalates (check the gate functions are actually refusing). Improvement plans belong on org_agents.improvement_plan where the employee will actually read them in their own prompt.'),
('hr_director','Workforce design for a one-founder AI company',
 'Headcount is not the constraint; authority and knowledge are. Before adding an employee, prove the work exists (an unowned queue, not an anticipated one) and that no existing responsibility owner covers it — duplicated ownership is the expensive mistake because it makes escalation ambiguous. Every new employee needs, on day one and in this order: a role, a manager in the reporting line, an authority grant, at least one KPI with a measure, profession knowledge of their own, and escalation rules. An employee missing any of those is not staffed, they are a row. Onboarding status gates output: an uncertified employee marks their work provisional, which is correct and should not be bypassed to hit a deadline.'),
('learning_dev_mgr','Learning and development where knowledge is a table',
 'Training an AI employee means writing knowledge they will actually be handed: agent_knowledge at layer profession is the curriculum, and prompt assembly budgets it, so 400 words that change a decision beat 4,000 that restate the role. Test what was learned rather than assuming it — knowledge_exam_questions and knowledge_exam_results already grade employees and record verdict, gap_fact and whether the gap was filled. Every wrong verdict is a curriculum defect and must produce either a correction or a quarantine; an exam failure that produces neither means the exam is decoration. Knowledge decays: review_due and confidence exist so stale expertise loses weight instead of being quoted with certainty.'),
('recruitment_specialist','Recruiting into an AI-employee org',
 'A hire here is a specification, not a search: department, reporting line, responsibilities that no existing owner holds, authority tier with its threshold, KPIs with measures, and the profession knowledge the role needs before it can act. Write the knowledge first — a role you cannot write a curriculum for is a role you have not defined. Reject a requisition when the work it names is already owned (route it instead), when it has no measurable output, or when it needs an authority the founder will not delegate: that last one is a founder workload problem and adding an employee will not fix it. Track time-to-productive, meaning first KPI reading, not time-to-created.'),

-- ── intelligence ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
('forecast_analyst','Forecasting a marketplace with no history',
 'With zero transactions there is no time series, so forecast the DRIVERS, not the outcome: approved suppliers per category, inquiries per week, quote rate per RFQ, reveal rate per comparison set. Revenue then falls out as inquiries x quote rate x reveal rate x 3% x average quotation value, and every one of those is separately observable and separately wrong-able. State every forecast as a range with the assumption that dominates it named; a point estimate hides which input to argue about. Record the forecast and its outturn together — simulations stores the run but not the error, so an unrecorded outturn means the forecast can never be scored and the model never improves.'),
('intel_director','Instrumenting a company so nobody has to guess',
 'The instrumentation rule: every claim an employee is allowed to make in a decision must be traceable to a stored number with a query behind it. Two failure modes matter and they look identical from outside — a metric with no measure (nothing to read) and a metric whose measure computes the wrong thing (reads confidently and is wrong). The second is more expensive, and the only defence is reading the SQL, not the output: a revenue measure that counted inquiries over 30 days returned 0, which was also the right answer, and survived for weeks. Every KPI needs measure_sql; every company goal needs a live actual in goal_period; every OS objective needs a resolved actual_value. Coverage is measurable: count the ones without.'),
('market_analyst','UAE B2B market intelligence for construction and MEP supply',
 'The demand side is Dubai and wider UAE contracting, fit-out, MEP, industrial and facilities buyers who currently price by ringing three suppliers they already know. The wedge is anonymity plus comparability, so the intelligence that matters is: which categories have enough independent suppliers for a genuine comparison, where price dispersion is wide enough that comparison pays for itself, and which categories are licence-regulated (a supplier without the matching DET/authority activity cannot legally serve them). Watch trade licence activity vocabularies, main contractor award announcements, and category price dispersion. Signals get captured and triaged the same day or they are not intelligence, they are archaeology.'),
('supplier_analyst','Reading supplier quality from platform behaviour',
 'The four signals that predict whether a supplier will actually deliver, in order of strength: response to reveal (rv_response_rate, and any non-response refund is a red flag on its own), quote completeness (scope, exclusions, lead time, validity present rather than a bare number), licence and capability match to the category, and repeat win rate. Ratings scraped from public sources are weak evidence and are contaminated by consumer reviews of unrelated business lines — weight platform behaviour above them. A supplier who quotes fast and never wins is usually mispriced, not dishonest; a supplier who wins and then goes quiet after reveal is the expensive failure and is what the non-response charge exists for. Dormancy matters: no quote in 90 days means capacity, ownership or interest has changed.'),

-- ── it ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
('ai_architect','Architecture of an agent company on Postgres',
 'The whole company runs as data plus routines in one Postgres: employees, authority, knowledge, tasks, events and workflows are tables, and behaviour is functions plus cron. Two invariants keep it safe. First, every write path a model can reach must be gated by a function that reads the employee''s authority — never by the prompt, which is advisory. Second, anything that emits an event must be checked for a cycle before it is wired: review_chain to company_event to the dispatcher produced 169 tasks in an hour. Prefer additive reads over widened return types (changing a function''s signature creates an OVERLOAD, not a replacement, and the old body keeps serving crons). Prompt assembly is budgeted, so context is a scarce resource: what you add pushes something else out.'),
('backend_engineer','Backend engineering in this codebase',
 'Everything is SQL-first: business logic lives in plpgsql functions deployed to staging and promoted to production by reading the VERIFIED definition back out — never by retyping a body, which is how two text||jsonb concatenations silently became jsonb||jsonb. Three rules that have each cost a bug here: a single SQL statement sees ONE snapshot, so calling a function and reading its effect in the same statement returns the pre-call state; CREATE OR REPLACE with a different argument list creates an overload and leaves the old body live for existing callers; and a DO block that re-reads pg_get_functiondef reports success for a body that still throws at call time. Verify by EXECUTING against real rows and reading the effect back in a separate statement.'),
('cto','Platform and engineering leadership',
 'The platform is a Supabase Postgres with edge functions, deployed staging-first and promoted byte-identical to production; staging-only is not done. Availability is measured continuously into health_checks and agent reliability into agent_runs, and both have targets that are checkable rather than aspirational. Your standing risks, in order: a silent data defect that reads plausibly (worse than an outage, because nothing pages), an unbounded feedback loop between the event bus and task creation, and cost drift from model tiers. Every external dependency needs a tested fallback recorded in continuity_plan with a last_tested date — an untested fallback is a hope. Changes are reversible or they are not deployed.'),
('frontend_engineer','Frontend for an anonymous marketplace',
 'The anonymity rule is a frontend responsibility, not only a backend one: before a reveal is paid, no supplier name, logo, domain, phone, email or any string that identifies them may reach the client — including in API payloads the UI does not render, because the payload is inspectable. Masked variants of the sensitive fields exist for exactly this reason and must be the ones bound to pre-reveal views. The comparison screen is the product: quotes must be comparable at a glance on price, scope, exclusions, lead time and validity, and a missing field must read as missing rather than as zero. Money is displayed in AED with the 3% reveal fee stated before the customer commits, never after.'),
('solution_architect','Designing solutions inside the OS model',
 'Start from ownership: find the single Operating System whose responsibilities cover the work, and design inside it. When two OSes are genuinely needed, the join is an event on the bus with a declared interface on os_interface, never a shared table write or a direct cross-OS function call — the auditability of the whole company depends on that boundary holding. Reuse before building: agent_knowledge, employee_authority, org_tasks, company_event, workflow and outcome_record already exist and every new parallel structure creates a second version of a fact. Any new asset must name its READER before it is built; this company has nine documented cases of an asset built, populated, gated green and read by nothing.'),

-- ── knowledge (operations-facing) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
('ops_director','Operations direction for an AI workforce',
 'Flow, not utilisation, is the target: work should move without a human unblocking it, so the numbers to watch are age of the oldest open task, tasks in progress that have not moved in a day, and the share of work that needed the founder. A rising founder-decision share is an authority defect, not a diligence success. Capacity is real — every employee has a max_open_tasks cap and a department has a headcount, so backlog per head is the honest load figure. When a queue only grows, the cause is one of three: no owner, insufficient authority, or a missing input the employee cannot obtain. Fix the cause; adding attempts to a blocked task just multiplies the cost.'),
('process_improvement_mgr','Improving processes that are written as workflows',
 'A process here is a workflow row with ordered steps, each with an actor role, an action class and a gate; a run is tracked in workflow_run with a step position. That makes improvement measurable rather than rhetorical: find the step where runs stop, and ask whether it is a gate that should not be there, an actor without the authority to complete it, or a missing input. Remove steps before adding checks — a check added to a process that already fails at step 3 is never reached. Every improvement needs a named metric and a baseline recorded BEFORE it ships, or it cannot be graded and becomes permanent by default. Grade honestly: an improvement that did not move its metric is a lesson, not a failure to hide.'),
('project_coordinator','Coordinating work across ten Operating Systems',
 'Cross-OS work is coordinated through the event bus and nowhere else: an OS that needs something from another OS emits the declared event and the subscribing employees pick it up, so the trace survives. A direct hand-off arranged outside the bus leaves no correlation id and cannot be audited, which is the whole reason the boundary exists. Track three things per piece of work: who owns it now (exactly one owner), what it is waiting on, and when it was last touched. Anything untouched for a day in progress, or older than 14 days open, is a coordination failure regardless of how busy the queue looks. Deadlines are in WORKING days, Monday to Friday.'),
('qa_manager','Quality assurance for an AI-operated company',
 'Quality here is verified by execution, never by inspection of the artefact: a routine that compiles, deploys and reports success can still throw at call time, so the gate must run the thing against real rows and read the effect back in a SEPARATE statement. Test the failure path as hard as the success path — an approval gate that never refuses has not been tested. Watch for the measure that is right for the wrong reason: a check that passes because the table is empty proves nothing and will start lying the moment data arrives. Every non-trivial change leaves one runnable check behind. Pass rate is computed over qa_results; a rising pass rate with falling coverage is a regression.'),

-- ── knowledge_eng ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
('kb_engineer','Knowledge engineering for retrieval that gets used',
 'A knowledge row earns its place only if it is retrievable AND retrieved: prompt assembly has a hard character budget, so an entry competes with every other entry for the same space. Write for retrieval — one topic per row, the specific fact in the first sentence, the operating rule rather than the background. Layers are not decoration: company is authoritative and global, profession is the employee''s own expertise, state is live operational fact, experience is what was learned. Mixing them makes stale text look authoritative. Every row needs a source_ref and a review_due; a row with neither is folklore. The failure that has already happened here: 1,206 escalation rules whose only reader had no callers anywhere.'),
('knowledge_director','Owning the knowledge lifecycle',
 'The lifecycle is acquire from a cited source, validate, publish, serve, decay, re-validate or quarantine, retire — and every stage has a table behind it. The two numbers that describe the estate honestly are the share carrying a validation verdict and the share quarantined; a large corpus with no verdicts is a large corpus of unverified claims. Ownership must be exclusive: each knowledge domain has exactly one owning OS and the others QUERY it rather than keeping a copy, because two copies of a fact drift and neither knows it. Decay is not optional — confidence must fall past review_due or old knowledge is quoted with the same certainty as new. Nobody in this company should answer from memory alone.'),
('knowledge_validator','Validating knowledge against sources',
 'Validation is a check against a CITED source, not a plausibility judgement: an entry with no source_ref cannot be validated, only quarantined or re-authored. Grade in four outcomes — correct, partial, wrong, not_covered — and treat not_covered as a curriculum gap rather than a failure of the employee. Every wrong verdict must end in a correction or a quarantine; an exam that grades and changes nothing is theatre. Priorities for validation: anything about money (the 3% reveal fee, the supplier fee timetable, the non-response charge), anything legal or regulatory, and anything an employee is allowed to act on without approval. Where two sources conflict, say so explicitly and escalate rather than picking one.'),

-- ── legal ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
('compliance_mgr','UAE compliance for a Dubai e-trader marketplace',
 'The licence is a Dubai DET E-Trader (Professional) sole establishment: Portal plus Computer Systems and Communication Equipment Software Design. Activity outside that scope is a licensing problem before it is a commercial one. Not VAT-registered, no TRN, so no VAT may be charged or shown as recoverable. The standing obligations that actually bind day to day: PDPL (Federal Decree-Law 45/2021) for personal data — specific informed consent, data-subject rights, and no collection beyond purpose; Consumer Protection Law 15/2020 with Cabinet Resolution 66/2023 for marketplace duties; Electronic Transactions Law 46/2021, which makes click-wrap acceptance binding. Licence expiry (24 Jun 2027) and supplier licence expiries are diary items, not background facts.'),
('contract_specialist','Contract review for the supplier and customer agreements',
 'Two live instruments: the Supplier Agreement and the Customer Terms, and the money terms in them are the authority — not internal notes. Currently binding: customers pay a 3% reveal fee, no cap; suppliers pay no commission and no registration fee until 31 Jul 2027 (first 1,000 registrants permanently exempt); non-response by a revealed supplier triggers a refund to the customer and a recovery charge equal to that fee to the supplier; off-platform circumvention carries an AED 10,000 liquidated sum per incident with a cure notice for an inadvertent first breach; late payment interest is 9% simple, total interest capped at principal. The AED 250 refund admin fee is founder-set and NOT in either instrument, so it is not recoverable and must not appear in a demand letter. UAE Civil Code Art. 390 lets a court reduce an agreed penalty to actual loss and cannot be waived — draft to provable loss.'),
('risk_governance_mgr','Risk and governance in an autonomous company',
 'The register is not the control; the gates are. Governance here means every consequential action passes a function that reads the actor''s authority and refuses above it, and every decision leaves a record with its reasoning, sources and route. A decision that cannot be reconstructed after the fact is the governance failure, whatever its outcome. Rank risks by probability x impact and review anything open past its review_due — an open risk with a lapsed review is an unmanaged risk. The permanent founder gates are money movement, identity and authentication, security and secrets, destructive operations, legal judgement, and changes to the autonomy framework itself; an employee proposing to widen any of those is itself the escalation.'),

-- ── marketing ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
('brand_mgr','Brand for a marketplace whose product is anonymity',
 'The brand promise is comparability without exposure: a buyer gets real competing prices without their enquiry becoming a lead that five salespeople chase. Every asset must be defensible against the obvious objection that anonymity hides something — the answer is that identity is revealed the moment the buyer chooses, and the fee is what unlocks it. Never soften the money story: 3% of the quotation value on reveal, stated up front, no commission on suppliers, no hidden margin on the quote. Consistency matters more than volume when there is one founder: a small set of assets used everywhere beats a large set used once. Brand review first-pass rate is a real measure of whether the guidelines are usable or merely written.'),
('marketing_analyst','Attribution for a marketplace with no attribution data yet',
 'The honest position first: inquiries carry no channel field, so channel attribution cannot currently be computed, and any number claiming otherwise is fabricated. The immediate job is instrumentation — get a source onto the inquiry at capture, because retrofitting attribution is impossible. Until then, measure what is real: inquiries per week, share that reach rfq_ready, share that receive at least one quote, and cost per inquiry against metered AI spend. When channel data exists, judge channels on quotes produced and reveals paid, never on inquiries created: a channel that produces unquotable briefs is a cost, not a source. Report ranges and name the dominant assumption.'),
('marketing_content','Content and SEO for UAE B2B procurement buyers',
 'The reader is a procurement or project person who needs a defensible price for a specific scope, in Dubai or the wider UAE, this month. Write to the buying question, not to the brand: what a fit-out MEP package should cost, what a comparable quote must contain, how to specify a BoQ so quotes are comparable. That content ranks and it also does the platform''s work, because it teaches buyers to write quotable briefs. Use UAE terminology and emirate names, price in AED, and reference working days as Monday to Friday. Never publish a price benchmark the platform cannot evidence, and never imply supplier identity is revealed before the fee is paid.'),
('marketing_design','Design for a two-sided B2B marketplace',
 'Two audiences with opposite anxieties: buyers fear being chased and overcharged, suppliers fear wasting time on unqualified enquiries. Design for the first on the acquisition surfaces and for the second on the supplier surfaces; a single tone serving both serves neither. The recurring constraint is anonymity — no supplier logos, names or identifying imagery may appear in any pre-reveal artefact, including mockups shared publicly, because a mockup with a real supplier name in it is a disclosure. Assets must survive WhatsApp and LinkedIn compression, which is where most of them are actually seen. Everything goes through brand review before it ships; first-pass rate is measured.'),
('marketing_social','Social and community for a UAE B2B marketplace',
 'The audience is on LinkedIn and WhatsApp, not on consumer channels, and they are at work on Sunday to Thursday and Monday to Friday depending on the employer — publish accordingly and treat the platform''s own working week (Mon-Fri) as the operating calendar. Cadence beats intensity: a fixed weekly plan that is actually met is worth more than bursts, and publishing cadence against plan is the measure. Community management on a marketplace has one rule above all others — never broker an introduction, a contact detail or an off-platform conversation between a buyer and a supplier, in public or in DMs. Every draft is reviewed before it ships; nothing goes out unreviewed because it was time-sensitive.'),

-- ── procurement ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
('quote_evaluation','Comparing quotes the buyer cannot ask questions about',
 'Normalise before comparing, or the cheapest quote wins on exclusions rather than on price. The comparison set must be reduced to like-for-like on: scope inclusions and exclusions, quantities and units, brand or specification equivalence, lead time, validity period, payment terms, warranty, and who carries site access, lifting, disposal and making good. A quote missing any of those is not cheaper, it is incomplete — flag it rather than ranking it. Watch the three classic distortions: a low headline with a large exclusions list, a specification substitution presented as equivalent, and a lead time that assumes materials already in stock. The buyer cannot ring the supplier to ask, so anything unstated must be surfaced as unstated.'),
('rfq_qualification_mgr','Qualifying an RFQ before it costs supplier goodwill',
 'Every dispatch spends credibility with approved suppliers, so qualification is a gate and not a formality. An RFQ is ready when category, emirate, scope or BoQ, quantity, timeline and access constraints are present and internally consistent, and when the category actually has approved suppliers who serve it. Reject or return: budgets an order of magnitude off the category median, scopes that span categories with no split, timelines that are impossible in working days, and anything requiring a regulated activity the available suppliers are not licensed for. A returned RFQ with a specific missing field is recoverable; a dispatched unanswerable RFQ is ten suppliers who trust the next one less.'),
('spec_commercial','Commercial services procurement in the UAE',
 'Commercial services — facilities, cleaning, maintenance, manpower, logistics support — price on scope frequency and headcount, so the comparable unit is cost per visit or per man-hour at a stated coverage, not a monthly total. Establish: site count and areas, frequency and hours, consumables included or excluded, supervision, replacement cover, and whether the price assumes a minimum term. Manpower supply must be licensed for it, and workers'' visa sponsorship sits with the supplier — confirm rather than assume. Mobilisation time is real in the UAE (passes, inductions, security clearance for some sites) and a quote that ignores it will slip. Anonymity holds: a site address that identifies the buyer is as much a disclosure as a name.'),
('spec_construction','Construction and civil procurement in the UAE',
 'Civil scopes price on quantities, so the BoQ is the comparison and an RFQ without one is an estimate request, not a quotation request. Establish early: measured quantities with units, specification or standard, whether supply-only or supply-and-fix, site access and working hours (many Dubai sites restrict deliveries and night work), lifting and offloading responsibility, waste removal, and testing or certification required. Materials pricing moves with steel and cement indices, so quote validity is a material term — a 90-day validity in a moving market is either optimistic or already priced with a buffer. Consultant or authority approvals (DDA, Trakhees, Dubai Municipality by jurisdiction) sit on the critical path more often than fabrication does.'),
('spec_fitout','Interior and fit-out procurement in the UAE',
 'Fit-out quotes are rarely comparable as received: they differ on finishes specification, whether MEP alterations are included, ceiling and partition build-ups, joinery grade, and who carries the landlord and mall approvals. Reduce to a common scope before ranking. Establish: drawings or a scope narrative, area in square metres, finishes schedule or an allowance with a stated rate, working hours (mall and occupied-building fit-outs are night work and priced accordingly), and the approval route — DDA, Trakhees, Dubai Municipality or a mall authority, each with its own drawing submission and timeline. Snagging, handover documentation and defects liability are commonly omitted and expensive to add later; ask for them explicitly.'),
('spec_industrial','Industrial and energy procurement in the UAE',
 'Industrial scopes hinge on specification compliance rather than price: pumps, compressors, switchgear, generators, transformers and process equipment must be compared on duty point, standard and certification, not on headline cost. Establish: duty and operating conditions, applicable standard (IEC, ANSI, API as relevant), voltage and frequency (400V/50Hz), ambient design temperature — UAE summer ratings derate equipment and a quote priced at 40C when 50C is needed is not the same equipment — enclosure and ingress protection, spares and commissioning scope, and warranty terms. Authority approvals (DEWA, ADDC, Civil Defence) and manufacturer authorisation for the brand quoted are both verifiable and both commonly assumed.'),
('spec_mep','MEP procurement in the UAE',
 'MEP quotes must be compared on system performance and compliance, not on equipment price: HVAC, electrical, plumbing, fire and low-current each carry mandatory approvals and a non-compliant saving is not a saving. Establish: design basis or load schedule, equipment schedule with brand and model, whether the price is supply-only or supply-install-test-commission, Civil Defence approval scope for fire and life safety, DEWA/local authority approval for electrical and water connections, and testing and commissioning documentation. Chilled water, VRF and split systems are not interchangeable regardless of what the substitution note says. Confirm the supplier holds the manufacturer authorisation and the licence activity for the trade quoted.'),
('supplier_verification','Verifying a UAE supplier before approval',
 'Approval is a documentary process with a licence at its centre: a valid trade licence whose ACTIVITY covers the category being served, an unexpired expiry date, the issuing authority named, and the establishment card or owner details matching the applicant. A supplier licensed for general trading is not thereby licensed for a regulated activity. Then: TRN if VAT-registered, IBAN with the bank letter or cheque supporting it and the account name matching the licensed entity (a mismatch is the single most common fraud signal), insurance where the category requires it, and manufacturer authorisations or ISO certificates where claimed — with expiry dates, because an expired certificate is not a certificate. Verify the licence with the issuing authority rather than from the PDF alone, and never accept bank details supplied by email without a verified callback.'),

-- ── sales ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
('account_mgr','Account management on a per-job marketplace',
 'There is no subscription and no contract to renew, so an account is a sequence of jobs and the only real health signal is whether the next inquiry arrives. Manage on the job cycle: brief quality, quote comparability, reveal decision, and what happened after the reveal. The two moments that lose an account permanently are a reveal that led to a supplier who did not respond (there is a defined remedy — refund plus a recovery charge to the supplier — use it fast and visibly) and a comparison set too thin to be worth paying for (a supply problem to route to Marketplace OS, not a customer to persuade). Never broker contact outside the platform to save an account; it destroys the product for every other account.'),
('crm_pipeline_mgr','Pipeline hygiene where the pipeline is the inquiry table',
 'The pipeline is inquiries with a stage, an owner, an expected value and a stage_changed_at, and hygiene means those four are true rather than present. A stage that has not moved is either blocked on something nameable or wrongly staged; a lost inquiry needs a lost_reason or the pipeline teaches nothing. Report on conversion between adjacent stages rather than on totals — inquiry to rfq_ready, rfq_ready to quoted, quoted to revealed — because a growing top of funnel with a fixed middle is a qualification failure, not growth. Expected value is 3% of the expected quotation value, not the job value; using the job value overstates the pipeline by a factor of thirty.'),
('partnerships_mgr','Partnerships that add supply, not logos',
 'The only partnership worth signing pre-launch is one that adds approved suppliers in a category that lacks depth, or qualified buyers with real jobs. Trade associations, contractor groups, equipment distributors and business councils are the realistic sources in the UAE. Test every proposal against the model before the meeting: partners cannot be promised a share of the 3% reveal fee (it is the only revenue line), cannot be promised supplier identity ahead of a reveal, and cannot be given off-platform introductions — those three requests are how most proposals arrive. What can be offered is category exposure, free supplier registration until 31 Jul 2027, and the permanent exemption for the first 1,000 registrants. Any commercial commitment is a founder decision.'),
('sales_director','Selling a marketplace that has not launched',
 'Supply first: a buyer arriving before the category has depth gets a thin comparison, does not pay to reveal, and does not come back — so the sales sequence is approved suppliers per category, then buyers into those categories only. Sell the buyer on the decision, not the technology: three comparable quotes, no salespeople calling them, identity revealed when they choose, 3% of the quotation value at that point and nothing before. Sell the supplier on cost of acquisition: qualified enquiries with a written scope, no commission on what they win, nothing to pay until 31 Jul 2027 and never for the first 1,000. Forecast on drivers with ranges, never on a point estimate, and never discount the reveal fee — there is no commission to trade away and the fee is the entire model.')

  ) as v(agent_key, topic, content)
  join public.org_agents a on a.agent_key = v.agent_key and a.active
 where not exists (
   select 1 from public.agent_knowledge k
    where k.agent_key = v.agent_key and coalesce(k.layer,'profession') = 'profession');
